  "Raster re-extracted independently from the PDF (xref 269, DeviceGray 1506x723, placed at bbox 117.02,295.97,478.46,469.49 pt on page 13).",
  "Calibration re-derived from the OUTWARD TICK MARKS (darkness-weighted centroids of the tick stubs below the x axis and left of each panel's y axis), not from spines/gridlines as the extractor did. x ticks (raster px) alpha=1: 109.96,190.92,271.87,352.79,433.73,514.52; alpha=5: 595.32..1000.03; alpha=10: 1080.94..1485.31 for beta=15,30,...,90 -> 5.3946/5.3961/5.3919 px/deg, max residual 0.014 deg. y ticks: 13.32,100.87,188.50,276.19,363.68,451.35 for Gamma=5..0 -> 87.608 px per unit Gamma, max residual 0.0008. Both axes linear (equal tick spacing), units degrees and dimensionless. Agrees with the extractor's 5.395 px/deg and 87.63 px/Gamma.",
  "Solid curves: sub-pixel run mid-points (threshold 128, linear edge interpolation) by columns where shallow and by rows where steep; at each knot beta0 two INDEPENDENT one-sided straight-line fits over [beta0-4.5,beta0-0.7] and [beta0+0.7,beta0+4.5] deg are evaluated at beta0 (no global piecewise model). Left and right extrapolations agree to <=0.005 at nearly all knots, which independently confirms that the plotted polylines have vertices at the 5-deg values.",
  "Dashed curves: each dash isolated as a connected component; end caps trimmed by t*sin(theta)+2 px using the dash's PCA axis; one-sided line fits as above (windows [beta0-4.9,beta0-0.6] / [beta0+0.6,beta0+4.9]). Additionally, for dashes lying entirely within one 5-deg interval, the dash centroid + principal axis was extended to the knot (another independent estimate; agrees within 0.02).",
  "alpha=1, beta>83.8 (dashed touches solid): solid centre from the merged run's lower edge minus half the nominal solid run height (7.03 px), dashed centre from the upper edge plus half the nominal dashed run height; segment fits extrapolated to 85 and 90.",
  "Crossing of Gamma=5 re-measured from row mid-points near the top: 22.41, 26.57, 27.21, 33.51, 30.46, 34.81 deg (ref 22.46, 26.46, 27.2, 33.3, 30.5, ~34.4; dashed crossings differ by 0.1-0.4 deg because only a short top dash fragment exists, as the ref says)."
 ],
 "series_identification": "Confirmed from the legend inside the raster: solid line = 'Seepage Forces -grad u'_FE', dashed line = 'Seepage Forces K . v'_opt' (legend prints K double-underlined . v'_opt; the body text writes the approximation as -grad u ~ K^-1 . v'_opt - the ref uses the legend wording, which is correct for labelling). Panels alpha=1,5,10 left to right confirmed from the in-panel boxes. Dashed above solid everywhere and both increase with alpha, consistent with the text (p13: higher alpha -> higher stability factors).",
 "nulls_checked": "All null entries are correct: no curve inside the axes at beta=15,20 (except alpha=1 solid which enters at 22.4 deg, so 20 is null); alpha=1 dashed 25, alpha=5 solid 25, alpha=5 dashed 30, alpha=10 solid 30 (crossing at 30.46 deg -> Gamma(30)~5.17>5) and alpha=10 dashed 30 are above Gamma=5.",
